[{"id":"x-predict-q","itemId":"unknown-value","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"X is drawn hatched. This is a second copy of lesson 3.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">pin_hold</code>, with its own inputs: at a rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>; otherwise it keeps its value. <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> has no reset, so until its first load the simulator shows X. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> for the rest: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> is first 1 at the edge that starts cycle 3, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> stays X until then, even while <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> changes: with <code class=\"nobreak\">load</code> at 0, no line gives <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> a value. Then <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> takes 0, keeps it in cycle 4, takes 1 in cycle 5, keeps it in cycle 6, and takes 0 in cycle 7. On the board this <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> would start at 0; the X says only that the code never said (lesson 3.2).</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"pin-hold-q","source":"hdl/level-03/pin_hold/pin_hold_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"pin_hold_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"load","path":"pin_hold_tb.load2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"pin_hold_tb.d2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[7.5,"1"]]},{"label":"q","path":"pin_hold_tb.dut2.q","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"],[3,"0"],[5,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["x","x","x","0","0","1","1","0"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"q","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"x-predict-siren","itemId":"unknown-value","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 0.2's alarm: <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code>armed &amp; opening</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is <code>door_open | window_open</code>. The testbench leaves <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> at X, as if nothing had set it. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> for each step: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p>With the door and the window both closed, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is 0, and X &amp; 0 is 0 whatever X is: <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is 0 in steps 0, 2, 5 and 7. With either one open, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is 1, and X &amp; 1 is X: the simulator cannot say whether the siren sounds, because nobody said whether the alarm is armed (lesson 3.2).</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"alarm-x-armed","source":"hdl/level-03/alarm_x/alarm_x_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"alarm_x_tb.armed","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.door_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[3,"1"],[5,"0"]]},{"label":"siren","path":"alarm_x_tb.siren","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"x"],[2,"0"],[3,"x"],[5,"0"],[6,"x"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["0","x","0","x","x","0","x","0"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"siren"},{"id":"x-find-bug","itemId":"unknown-value","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"At a rising edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> should clear all four bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>; otherwise <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>. The testbench fails, and the waveform shows <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> as X after the first reset. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>q[1:0] &lt;= 2'b00;</code> gives a value only to bits 1 and 0 (a part-select, lesson 1.1). Bits 3 and 2 get none at the first reset, so they stay X (lesson 3.2), and after a later reset they keep whatever they held. The first failure is <code>q=xx00, expected 0000 at 10 ns</code>. Written <code>if (rst) q &lt;= 4'b0000;</code>, the reset clears all four bits. The <code class=\"nobreak\">else</code> line is right: it loads all four.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-03/reg4_bug/reg4_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A 4-bit register with a synchronous reset: at a rising edge, rst clears","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// all four bits of q; otherwise q takes d.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"reg4_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       rst,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst) q[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2'b00","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"     q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":10,"fixLine":"if (rst) q <= 4'b0000;"},{"id":"x-predict-door","itemId":"unknown-value","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 0.2's alarm: <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code>armed &amp; opening</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is <code>door_open | window_open</code>. The testbench sets <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">window_open</code>, but leaves <code class=\"nobreak\">door_open</code> at X, as if nothing had set it. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> for each step: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p>Work from the inside out. With the window open, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is X | 1, which is 1 whatever X is, so <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code>: 1 in steps 1, 4 and 7, and 0 in steps 3 and 6. With the window closed, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is X | 0, which is X; then <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is X where <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> is 1 (steps 0 and 5), and 0 where <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> is 0 (step 2), because 0 &amp; X is 0 (lesson 3.2).</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"alarm-x-door","source":"hdl/level-03/alarm_x/alarm_x_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"alarm_x_tb.armed","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.door_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"]]},{"label":"siren","path":"alarm_x_tb.siren","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"x"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["x","1","0","0","1","x","0","1"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"siren"},{"id":"x-order-debug","itemId":"unknown-value","role":"core","promptHtml":"In a simulation of lesson 0.2's alarm, <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is X in some steps. Put these steps in order to find out why.","explanationHtml":"<p>Start where the problem first shows, then follow the X back through the line that makes it, one signal at a time, as lesson 0.4 followed a wrong value back from a TEST FAILED line. Here the trail ends at a signal nobody set, one of lesson 3.2's causes of X. Changing the testbench before you know which signal is X would be a guess.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Find the first step in which `siren` is X.","Look at the line that drives `siren`, and at the signals it reads.","Find which of those signals is X in that step: `armed`.","Look for the line in the testbench that sets `armed`, and find none.","Make the testbench set `armed`, then run the simulation again."],"shuffled":[0,3,2,1,4]}]